      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-259421",
      ":question/problem": "Prove that if $151$ numbers are selected from the set ${1, 2, \u2026, 300}$, then two of the chosen numbers must sum to $301$.\n\nLet's partition the set ${1, 2, \u2026, 300}$ into\n{{field-1}}\nsubsets, each containing\n{{field-2}}\nelements such that the sum of elements in each subset equals\n{{field-3}}, as follows:\n\n${1, 300}, {2, 299}, {3, 298}, \u2026, {150, 151}$."
